  "findings": [
    {
      "blocking": false,
      "detail": "The compact shoulders, low collar, plain breastplate, modest cross, leather guards and short russet cloth form a clearly simpler secondary set. It remains a stylized game asset rather than photographic realism."
    },
    {
      "blocking": false,
      "detail": "Rolled steel edges, fitted hinge tabs and rivets, folded plate returns, binding straps, sewn boot welts and turned cloth hems add construction detail. Metal roughness, leather grain and cloth weave remain subtle at gameplay scale."
    },
    {
      "blocking": false,
      "detail": "The initial boot audit found 3.313 mm clearance in late death. A leather toe rand restores the accepted contact footprint: the final measured maximum is 1.124 mm. The actual re-export audit has zero errors and warnings; no animation or shared body/weapon bytes were changed."
    },
    {
      "blocking": false,
      "detail": "A closeup found the independently moving lower shoulder lame cutting through its compact cap in melee. The cap, lame and fastening hardware now share the shoulder attachment, preserving their overlap. The final Cycles closeup verifies the correction separately from the workbench diagnostics."
    },
    {
      "blocking": false,
      "detail": "All nine clips were inspected at three phases and targeted grip/death views. Sampled motion diagnostics are not an exhaustive certificate for all possible animation blends. The inherited death clip folds forward rather than ending fully prone."
    },
    {
      "blocking": false,
      "detail": "Neutral and material views and all three LODs were inspected. LOD1/2 simplify trim, hands and badge detail; current runtime continues to select LOD0. No automatic distance switching is added."
    },
    {
      "blocking": false,
      "detail": "Additive local installation only: nine catalog items and preview selection. Existing saved equipment, ornate armor, inventory and starter loadout remain unchanged. No deployment or new acquisition system is included."
    }
  ],
